<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3f2662552630b0ff08f2f5e0a65377f770baf80a" commit="f0ad37f6215e1a454851321d0e25fa467b416ed0" commit_message="chromeos-config: Remove dep on chromeos-config-models.  Remove dependency on virtual/chromeos-config-models and adjust the UB install_private_model_files functions.  Correct cros-model.eclass to new structure of model files being in chromeos-config-bsp, and actual config files in chromeos-bsp-&lt;board&gt;.  Includes workaround code in cros-unibuild.eclass to always put coral first in the get_dtb_data function, so the resulting shellball will only have the one shared bios.bin.  BUG=b:67313978,b:68219217,b:68219319,b:68219365,b:68219002,b:68218912 TEST=unmerge all bsp packages, then emerge-coral chromeos-config      and check all dependencies are being built and conf. files installed.      build_packages &amp;&amp; build_image CQ-DEPEND=CL:*486337  Change-Id: I3f2662552630b0ff08f2f5e0a65377f770baf80a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/731778 Commit-Ready: Patrick Berny &lt;pberny@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Patrick Berny &lt;pberny@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Patrick Berny &lt;pberny@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="731778" owner_email="pberny@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="13" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/78/731778/13" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib1c604b29e7f0e47cc036e042fe597f644d7ad36" commit="cf4968089dffa3cf34f719a1a7111fc62867f6ed" commit_message="driver: Rename pmic_tps650830 -&gt; pmic_tps650x30.  The registers seem to be the same for the TPS650930, therefore, this commit just renames the register map to have a more generic name.  BUG=None BRANCH=None TEST=make -j buildall  Change-Id: Ib1c604b29e7f0e47cc036e042fe597f644d7ad36 Signed-off-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/736311 Commit-Ready: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="736311" owner_email="aaboagye@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/11/736311/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8924320030a00b8808aea27fb668451e6e41d590" commit="e42670adf464a6f045418602d6def19543634f0f" commit_message="zoombini: cannonlake: Add 5V power good signal.  The 5V power good signal is being removed from the PMIC power good tree, however, if the 5V power good is not asserted, we should not try booting to S0.  This is because the 1050_STG rail load switch is powered off of the 5V rail.  Since wireless power control is being moved to the AP, these pins are now repurposed to control the PMIC enable and for the 5V power good signal.  This commit adds the 5V power good pin to the EC and makes it a required power signal for S0.  BUG=b:66000679 BRANCH=None TEST=make -j buildall TEST=flash zoombini;  Verify EC boots up okay.  Change-Id: I8924320030a00b8808aea27fb668451e6e41d590 Signed-off-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/736312 Commit-Ready: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="736312" owner_email="aaboagye@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/12/736312/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I29a300247e4a2359b98d3546de7a024fd111958e" commit="1d5c693fe06e3e53a08aad34b09c5f38bc4c4da5" commit_message="zoombini: Add PMIC init.  Currently, the only we init we need to do is mask VCCIO and 5VA from the power good tree.  Additionally, we deassert PMIC_EN for 30ms during boot.  BUG=b:66000679, b:66975317, b:66952064 BRANCH=None TEST=Flash zoombini;  Verify that PMIC initializes okay.  Change-Id: I29a300247e4a2359b98d3546de7a024fd111958e Signed-off-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/736313 Commit-Ready: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="736313" owner_email="aaboagye@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/13/736313/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia772121774236ee056ab0961e0e000f16c1476ce" commit="ccfb95cece83060dc45d335eea958f85d5202676" commit_message="shill: make property identifier for Cellular.ModelID consistent  This doesn't follow the style guide, so add another identifier that does and a note to remove the other one later.  BUG=None TEST=emerge  Change-Id: Ia772121774236ee056ab0961e0e000f16c1476ce Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/738457 Commit-Ready: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="738457" owner_email="ejcaruso@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/system_api" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/system_api" ref="refs/changes/57/738457/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1a8501d1ba75d1ad7fc5bb9c90f3861afab5e025" commit="0c4cf493fe985c99f8cab2f750ff38d87c5d6e23" commit_message="shill: Use correct casing for Cellular.ModelID property  The style guide says acronyms should be cased as if they were words, and we already do this for several of the other acronym properties on cellular Device objects, so just make things consistent here.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:738457 BUG=None TEST=emerge  Change-Id: I1a8501d1ba75d1ad7fc5bb9c90f3861afab5e025 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/738459 Commit-Ready: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="738459" owner_email="ejcaruso@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="aosp/platform/system/connectivity/shill" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/aosp/platform/system/connectivity/shill" ref="refs/changes/59/738459/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I98346c2c63c3665fa82c8258475ccf7253911742" commit="dfc4235fda11842b00185fff386cb7abba19384e" commit_message="cros-kernel: rockchip: Add SELINUX + other stuff to fallback defconfig  This enables SELINUX when building upstream kernels, which allows them to boot Chrome OS images.  It also gets other things setup to boot more modern kernel versions.  Much of this just came from matching up with the rockchip64_defconfig.  This is a relatively clean &quot;defconfig&quot; against v4.14-rc6 to avoid some of the old cruft.  It's possible that this defconfig won't work on some older kernels (if something was needed there that's now the default), but given how broken the old defconfig was I don't think it matters much.  Better to get out the cruft.  BUG=None TEST=Boot upstream kernel to login prompt, use USB.  Change-Id: I98346c2c63c3665fa82c8258475ccf7253911742 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/738752 Commit-Ready: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;diande